From 649768f4af29060b01965cf07a234def766c8875 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kenny Glowner <SisyphusAeolides@pm.me>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 08:33:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Input: elan_i2c - recover stalled controllers in place

Some Elantech controllers remain registered after a report-stream fault but
stop delivering usable input. Driver unbind and bind recovers the controller,
but replaces its input devices and invalidates userspace file descriptors.

Add a root-writable recovery attribute and an opt-in report-driven watchdog.
The watchdog is enabled by default on the Lenovo ThinkPad P53, runs only while
an input node is open, and recovers after three consecutive report-read
errors. It performs no periodic controller I/O, so healthy active and idle
controllers are untouched. Export successful report and error counts for
userspace diagnostics.

Release active input state before recovery and retain the registered input
objects throughout. Serialize recovery with firmware, calibration, suspend,
and resume operations. Include the substantive ELAN fixes through Linux 7.1
while retaining source compatibility with Linux 6.12.

Signed-off-by: Kenny Glowner <SisyphusAeolides@pm.me>
